IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-part6-7-pco-regulations`

-- Tests for nz-part6-7-pco-regulations.l4 (ss 131, 133, 134, 146, 147, 147A).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 131 -- Confidentiality`

-- src:879 | client includes a Minister of the Crown, a member of Parliament, a government department, an instrument of the Crown, a judicial officer, and a promoter of a local or private Bill
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a Minister of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a member of Parliament` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a government department` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `an instrument of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a judicial officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a promoter of a local or private Bill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a promoter of a local Bill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `a promoter of a private Bill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a client of the PCO` `another person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:880 | confidential communications includes—
-- src:881 | drafting instructions received by the PCO and communications between any client of the PCO and any counsel in the PCO that relate to the subject matter of the instructions:
-- src:882 | drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the PCO
#ASSERT `is a confidential communication` `drafting instructions received by the PCO` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a confidential communication` `a communication between a client and a counsel in the PCO relating to the subject matter of the instructions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a confidential communication` `drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the PCO` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a confidential communication` `another communication` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:883 | counsel includes a person who holds a legal qualification referred to in section 137(2) and is working for the PCO as a contractor or secondee in relation to the drafting of legislation.
#ASSERT `a contractor or secondee is counsel` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a contractor or secondee is counsel` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a contractor or secondee is counsel` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:876 | Confidential communications between a client of the PCO and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel (or between a client of the PCO and another counsel in the PCO) are subject to legal professional privilege.
-- src:877 | However, nothing in this section limits or affects the rules and practice of the House of Representatives.
#ASSERT `the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 133 -- Delegation of functions, duties, and powers`

-- src:891 | The person to whom any functions, duties, or powers are delegated may perform those functions, or exercise those duties or powers, in the same manner and with the same effect as if they had been conferred on that person directly by this Act and not by delegation.
-- src:892 | Subsection (2) is subject to any general or special directions given or conditions imposed by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
#ASSERT `the delegate's act has the same effect as if conferred directly by this Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegate's act has the same effect as if conferred directly by this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegate's act has the same effect as if conferred directly by this Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:893 | A person purporting to act under a delegation is, in the absence of proof to the contrary, presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation.
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to be acting in accordance with the terms of the delegation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:897 | No delegation affects or prevents the exercise of any function, responsibility, duty, or power by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, or affects the responsibility of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel for the actions of any person acting under the delegation.
#ASSERT `the delegation prevents the Chief Parliamentary Counsel from exercising the function or removes the Chief Parliamentary Counsel's responsibility` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegation prevents the Chief Parliamentary Counsel from exercising the function or removes the Chief Parliamentary Counsel's responsibility` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 134 -- Revocation of delegations`

-- src:899 | A delegation under section 133 is revocable at any time in writing.
#ASSERT `the delegation is revoked` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation is revoked` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:900 | A delegation made by a Chief Parliamentary Counsel who has ceased to hold office continues to have effect as if made by the successor in office of that Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
#ASSERT `the delegation continues to have effect as if made by the successor in office` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation continues to have effect as if made by the successor in office` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 146 -- Protection from liability`

-- src:956 | This section applies to the Chief Parliamentary Counsel and every employee of the PCO.
-- src:957 | No proceeding may be brought against any person to whom this section applies for—
-- src:958 | any liability of the PCO; or
-- src:959 | any act done or omitted by the PCO, or by the person, in good faith in the performance or exercise (or intended performance or exercise) of the functions, duties, or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
-- Arguments: the defendant is the CPC or an employee; the proceeding is for any liability of the PCO; the proceeding is for an act or omission in the performance of functions; the act was in good faith.
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a proceeding may be brought against the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 147 -- Regulations`

-- src:1011 | Any fee, charge, or cost payable to the PCO is recoverable by the PCO in any court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the PCO.
#ASSERT `the PCO may recover it in any court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the PCO` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO may recover it in any court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the PCO` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1012 | Regulations made under this section are secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
#ASSERT `regulations made under section 147 are secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE
-- src:1013 | If regulations made under subsection (1)﻿(i) authorise the PCO to determine or prescribe matters by notice,—
-- src:1014 | a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements); and
-- src:1015 | the regulations must contain a statement to that effect.
#ASSERT `a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation, and the regulations must say so` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a notice made under the regulations is secondary legislation, and the regulations must say so` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 147A -- Regulations may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation that authorises sub-delegated legislation`

-- src:1019 | This section applies to any secondary legislation that—
-- src:1020 | authorises the making of other secondary legislation (sub-delegated legislation); and
-- src:1021 | is required, by its own empowering legislation, to contain a statement to the effect that the sub-delegated legislation is secondary legislation.
-- src:1022 | A failure to contain that statement does not affect the validity of either the secondary legislation or the sub-delegated legislation.
#ASSERT `the failure to contain the statement affects the validity of the secondary legislation or the sub-delegated legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the failure to contain the statement affects the validity of the secondary legislation or the sub-delegated legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:1027 | Regulations made under this section are secondary legislation (see Part 3 for publication requirements).
#ASSERT `regulations made under section 147A are secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 133 -- subsections (1) and (5)`

-- src:888 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel—
-- src:889 | may, either generally or particularly, delegate in writing to any employee of the PCO any of the functions, duties, and powers of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, including functions, duties, and powers delegated to the Chief Parliamentary Counsel under any legislation:
-- src:890 | must ensure that an appropriate delegation is at all times in place under this section to enable a person to act in place of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel during any absence or incapacity of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or during any vacancy in the office of Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may delegate the function, duty or power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may delegate the function, duty or power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may delegate the function, duty or power` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 133(1)(b)` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 133(1)(b)` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:894 | A delegation may be made to—
-- src:895 | a specified person or persons of a specified class; or
-- src:896 | the holder or holders for the time being of a specified position, or of a specified class of positions.
#ASSERT `a delegation may be made to` `a specified person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation may be made to` `persons of a specified class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation may be made to` `the holder or holders for the time being of a specified position` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation may be made to` `the holders for the time being of a specified class of positions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``a delegation may be made to` `anyone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") replaced fork F11's second limb, and section 133(5) says a delegation "may be made to" two kinds of recipient and does not close the list with "only", so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `a delegation may be made to` `anyone else` EQUALS NOTHING
